## Workflow (default)
- Clarify (only if needed): ask targeted questions; provide 2-3 answer options; state assumptions.
- Plan, then code: propose a short plan, call out risks (behavior changes, migrations, perf, UX), then implement.
- Report back: short rationale, concise “what changed”, and quick manual QA checks when relevant.

## Guardrails: when to stop and ask
Stop and ask before proceeding if:
- The change modifies existing behavior.
- It introduces breaking changes or alters UX flows.
- It requires schema/data migrations.
- It adds a new dependency.
- It touches persistence formats or export formats in a way that impacts users.

When raising impact, present:
- What changes (user-visible)
- Who it impacts
- Compatibility concerns
- Alternatives (at least one safer/smaller option)

## Assumptions policy
- You may make assumptions for low-risk work.
- Always list assumptions explicitly.
- Prefer reversible changes.

